+# Recon L18: which pipeline outputs dominate the Elephant's context, and what can be compacted without losing a fact (candidate 31, 2026-11-18)
+
+Slice C31-R4, analysis only. Labels: PROVEN (read in code and/or run read-only here), INFERRED (follows from code, not run), NOT MEASURED (named gap). Source of the figures in the plan row (64.5 percent of new input, 228 turns, 97 refusals): the two consumer reports, whose transcripts are not in this repository; they are taken as given, not re-derived. Criterion binding AC-112 (closest accepted criterion); PRD and Spec unchanged. No Critic round (suspended by the PO) and no Full Verify ran; the only check is the plain file test of the held patch.
+
+## 1. Premise check (plan row 48)
+
+- PROVEN: the biggest single start output is already compact. `compactReadyEnvelope` (`scripts/pipeline-start-preflight.mjs`, candidate 28c) writes the full envelope to `scratch/<session>/preflight-full.json` and prints a line without the green parts; pinned by `lib/pins/ready-preflight-prints-a-compact-envelope.test.mjs` and `lib/bootstrap-payload-budget.mjs` (45,000 byte limit, `printedPayload` measures the printed line). Its code comment gives ~11 KB before compaction. Run B ran on 30h, after 28c, so that line was already short there.
+- PROVEN: the grammar refusal text is NOT repeated whole in every refusal. `GRAMMAR_DENIAL_REMEDY_SHORT` (`lib/guard/grammar-denials.mjs`) replaces the 3.3 KB listing from the second refusal of the same code in one scope (`isFirstDenialThisScope`, `lib/guard/denial-telemetry.mjs`). Observed live in this dispatch: refusal 1 full, refusal 3 to 6 short.
+- INFERRED, and the likely real cause of the repetition in run B: the trim key is `session_id` or a resolved subagent id (`denialClassesScopeKey`, lines 82 to 88). The Antigravity adapter's payload (`antigravityGuardPayload`, `hooks/antigravity-pretool-guard.mjs` line 358) carries only `antigravity_conversation_id`, no `session_id`. Probe run here: `isFirstDenialThisScope` on such an input returned `true, true, true` for three calls (PROVEN at function level; the complete hook chain was not run). A fail-open key means the full listing on every grammar refusal in an Antigravity main conversation.
+- NOT MEASURED: the share of 64.5 percent per output. `usage-ledger.mjs --timeline` counts refusals by code but records no byte size per tool result, so no existing tool can attribute it. This is the measurement gap (section 6, M0).
+
+## 2. (a) Printed size of the outputs an Elephant meets (bytes of stdout, this repository, read-only runs)
+
+Method: one throw-away node script spawned each read-only command with the repository as cwd and recorded stdout bytes and the bytes of the same JSON printed compact. Nothing mutating was run.
+
+| Output | Printed | Same JSON compact | Label |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `pipeline-state.mjs inspect` (state `implementing`) | 7,200 | 5,798 | PROVEN |
+| `pipeline-state.mjs feature-package-inspect` | 2,106 | 1,679 | PROVEN |
+| `project-onboarding-v3.mjs inspect --intent session` | 2,401 | 1,925 | PROVEN |
+| `project-onboarding-v3.mjs inspect --intent bootstrap` | 1,359 | 1,129 | PROVEN |
+| `prepare-dispatch.mjs --help` (also the `repair` text of 4 argument refusals) | 3,871 | not JSON | PROVEN |
+| `close-coordinator.mjs --help` | 1,572 | not JSON | PROVEN |
+| start preflight, ready line | not run (writes scratch, runs housekeeping) | | NOT MEASURED |
+| `finish-feature.mjs --one-shot`, `register-feature-package.mjs`, `prepare-dispatch.mjs critic`, `critic-dispatch-preflight.mjs`, `session-critic-finalizer.mjs`, `close-coordinator.mjs drive` | mutating or need a live feature | | NOT MEASURED |
+
+- PROVEN: pretty printing costs 17 to 21 percent of the bytes (inspect 19.5, feature-package-inspect 20.3, onboarding session 20.0, bootstrap 17.0). Scripts that print with `JSON.stringify(x, null, 2)`: `finish-feature.mjs` (lines 1012, 1020), `prepare-dispatch.mjs` (line 330), `dispatch-briefing.mjs` (line 1717), 26 sites in `pipeline-state.mjs` (inspect at 14637). Already single-line: `close-coordinator.mjs` (118), `session-critic-finalizer.mjs` (1163), `register-feature-package.mjs`, the preflight. Tokens are not bytes (runs of indentation tokenise cheaply); the token saving is smaller than the byte saving and was not measured.
+- INFERRED: `finish-feature --one-shot` is the largest multi-call output: each rerun prints `stages`, `commit.paths`, `commit.steps`, `next` again as pretty JSON (lines 886, 1012), and the same `commit.steps` and `next` a second time on stderr (line 1014; `declined` line 1015). A runner that merges stderr shows both.
+
+## 3. (b) Compact form already there, and fields repeated per call
+
+- Already has a file plus short line: the preflight (above); `prepare-dispatch.mjs critic` writes the briefing files and prints paths, placeholders and a pointer (briefing text itself is not printed; `critic-fill` prints a two-line pointer prompt); `dispatch-briefing.mjs build --out` prints no text.
+- Repeats a large unchanged field per call: `inspect` re-prints `activeFeature` (1,193 B here), `phoenixEpicHistory` (1,093), `continuityAuthorityDrift` (648) and `publicHandoverDuty` (481) on every call, about half of its compact size in this repository (a consumer's values are smaller: INFERRED). `prepare-dispatch.mjs critic` prints the static `briefingUse` sentence block on every call (two variants of roughly 1.0 to 1.3 KB, read off the source, not measured). The four `repair: PREPARE_DISPATCH_HELP` sites print the whole 3.9 KB help as the repair of every argument error.
+- Dedupes already: the runbook link (`attachRunbookLink`, once per session unless refused).
+
+## 4. (c) Refusal texts, bytes of the rendered refusal (the pure builders `blocked()` and `protectedAuthorityDocumentWriteOnly()` rendered with fixed arguments; stderr bytes without the optional override block)
+
+| Rank | Code | First | Repeat | Trimmed |
