+| 5 | `GUARD-READ-SCOPE-OUTSIDE-ROOT` | 1,156 | 1,156 | no, by design (its remedy is the repair) |
+
+- PROVEN: the listing (`GRAMMAR_DENIAL_REMEDY`) is 3,345 B of every first refusal; the trimmed form is 280 B. Static literals of other refusal sites (INFERRED, approximate): `guard-gate-strength` about 1.4 KB, GIT-03 commit message about 1.4 KB, `guard-testpath` about 0.9 KB, `guard-push` target about 0.9 KB.
+- PROVEN, live in this dispatch: the trim key is the code, not the listing. A `GUARD-PARSE-UNSUPPORTED` refusal printed the whole listing, and the next call, a `GUARD-READ-COMMAND-UNSUPPORTED` refusal, printed it again in full, although the same listing was already in context. With four listing-printing codes a context window pays up to four full listings (about 14.7 KB), three more than needed (about 9.2 KB).
+- Frequency: 97 refusals in run A is from the report, not re-countable here. Rank 4 and 5 are rare or by design; ranks 1 to 3 are the frequent ones.
