+## 5. (d) Smallest builds, each failing-first, with the facts that must stay
+
+B1, refusal trim key (lib/guard/denial-telemetry.mjs, lib/guard/evaluate.mjs call sites, lib/guard/grammar-denials.mjs wording; clone-slice route, protected paths):
+- Change: `denialClassesScopeKey` falls back to `antigravity_conversation_id` when `session_id` and the subagent id are absent (same character check `^[A-Za-z0-9._-]{1,128}$` as `resetDenialClassesForSession`); the four listing-printing codes share one class key; the short text says "an earlier grammar refusal" instead of "of this kind".
+- Failing first (red today): in `denial-telemetry.test.mjs` an Antigravity-shaped input asked twice must give `true, false` (today `true, true`, probe above); code A then code B in one scope must render B short (today full).
+- Must stay: the first refusal in each scope is full (a fresh subagent has no earlier text); the `retryActions` JSON line, the `Rejected element` line and the request-bound `repeatOverrideGuidance` command stay in the short form; every failure of the store still fails open to the full text; no new file kind (the same `guard-denial-classes/<scope>.json` store holds one more key); `READ_SCOPE` and credential refusals unchanged.
+- Open: whether Antigravity has a post-compaction hook that must clear the conversation-keyed file like `resetDenialClassesForSession` does for Claude: NOT EXAMINED. Without it the short form could outlive a compaction on that runner.
+
+B2, single-line stdout for the four happy-path scripts (`pipeline-state.mjs inspect`, `finish-feature.mjs`, `prepare-dispatch.mjs`, `dispatch-briefing.mjs`): drop the indent argument at the five sites named in section 2 (17 to 21 percent of the bytes).
+- Failing first: a process test per script asserting that stdout is exactly one line and that `JSON.parse` gives the same value as today's output; red today (multi-line).
+- Must stay: every key and value, the exit codes, the stderr next-step lines. `lastJson()` in `prepare-dispatch.mjs` already parses a single line. Pins that match the multi-line text are restated (QG-04) and named.
+
+B3, `prepare-dispatch.mjs` argument refusals: `repair` names the usage line of the failed verb and `--help`, not the whole 3.9 KB help. Failing first: a refusal's `repair` must stay under 600 B and contain the verb's usage line. Must stay: a runnable command in `repair` (hard limit 4).
+
+B4, file plus short line for `inspect` and `finish-feature --one-shot`, in the shape of the preflight (full JSON beside the session scratch, printed line keeps `status`, `nextAction`, `next`, counts, and the path). NOT built here: the sizes of the second one are NOT MEASURED, so the gain is a guess until M0 ran on a transcript. Must stay (when built): `nextAction` and every `repair` verbatim in the printed line, and the file written only when the status is the success path, as `compactReadyEnvelope` does.
+
+M0, measurement: extend `usage-ledger.mjs --timeline` with the bytes of every tool result grouped by the script it ran (and by refusal code), derived from the transcript at read time, nothing stored. Failing first: a fixture transcript with two results of known size must list both under their script. This turns the 64.5 percent into a per-output table for all three runners and decides B4. It overlaps lane L17 (the same reader), so it should ride that slice.
+
+## 6. Ranked proposal
+
+1. B1: a proven defect on Antigravity (the trim never fires), about 3 KB saved per repeated grammar refusal, and about 9 KB per window on every runner from the shared key. Smallest, no new store, no gate.
+2. M0: the missing measurement, read-only, rides lane L17.
+3. B2: 17 to 21 percent of the bytes of the five largest happy-path outputs, mechanical.
+4. B3: small, removes the worst repeated static text of a script refusal.
+5. B4: only after M0 shows `inspect` or `finish-feature` carries a measurable share.
+Not proposed: a second shortened first print of the grammar listing (the first refusal must stay self-contained), trimming `GUARD-READ-SCOPE` (its text is the repair), any change to which refusal is raised.
+
+## 7. PO decisions, with defaults
+
+- D1: key the denial trim for Antigravity by the conversation id and share one key across the four listing codes (B1). Default: yes.
+- D2: also shorten the FIRST grammar refusal to a pointer to `templates/prompts/agent-obligations.md` section 1. Default: no (a consumer Elephant may not hold that file; the short form already points back to the first print).
+- D3: single-line JSON for the four happy-path scripts (B2). Default: yes; the 26 other `pipeline-state` sites stay.
+- D4: build M0 inside the L17 slice. Default: yes.
+- D5: B3 and B4. Default: B3 yes, B4 held until M0.
+
